very place the world let go of. Walk softly; most of them are sleeping.\""]},{"id":"charter-stone","x":120,"y":166,"title":"II. The Keepers' Charter","pages":["\"We do not undo the Drift. The Drift is the world breathing: what is let go makes room for what comes. We only remember.\"","\"And we built roads, so the lost could be visited. Not brought back. Visited. So a grandmother might stand once more in the square where she was born, and then come home.\""]},{"id":"stacks-stone","x":66,"y":140,"title":"III. On the Shelving of Places","pages":["\"Every place is shelved where it drifted from, and when. Some shelves are very long. Some places drift twice. Some, we think, drifted here from worlds that were never ours.\""]},{"id":"catalogue-stone","x":54,"y":84,"title":"IV. The Catalogue","pages":["\"Visitors to the gallery: the plates are shelved in catalogue order, as every keeper learns on the first day. A wrong plate returns the shelf to its start.\"","\"The catalogue reads: first the triangle, then the ring, then the moon, then the diamond, and last the star.\""]},{"id":"flood-stone","x":168,"y":146,"title":"V. The Flood","pages":["\"The Null found our roads. It does not walk; it spreads, and it spread along them, back toward the kept world. So we drowned the archive, to drown the roads' ink, and tore the index out of the Ledger.\"","\"Without the index the Ledger cannot be written in, and without the Ledger no road can open. That was the whole of our plan. It was a good plan, while it lasted.\""]},{"id":"carrel-stone","x":198,"y":98,"title":"VI. The Last Keeper's Note","pages":["\"Ondine stays. Someone must. I have hidden the last page where only someone looking very hard would find it.\"","\"If the Ledger is ever written in again, it will be by someone who does not know what it is. Forgive them, Ondine. Then stop them.\""]}],"spawns":[{"rect":[92,194,72,34],"species":["drowned-page"],"cap":3},{"rect":[14,118,70,64],"species":["drowned-page","ink-wraith"],"cap":4},{"rect":[30,56,60,52],"species":["ink-wraith","drowned-page"],"cap":3},{"rect":[160,112,30,30],"species":["ink-wraith"],"cap":2},{"rect":[104,96,48,34],"species":["null-shade","ink-wraith"],"cap":3},{"rect":[228,140,22,22],"species":["drowned-page"],"cap":2}],"plot":{"resident":{"name":"Ondine","x":130,"y":148,"look":"keeper"},"goal":"the Ledger of the Drift","relics":[{"id":"index-drowned","x":38,"y":132,"name":"Index of the Drowned"},{"id":"index-kept","x":243,"y":151,"name":"Index of the Kept"},{"id":"index-null","x":202,"y":98,"name":"Index of the Null"}],"talk":{"first":["Another reader. It has been so long. I am Ondine, last of the keepers. Mind the water: it is ink, mostly, and memory, and it does not forgive.","This is where we wrote down every place the world let go of. Not to bring them back. The Drift is the world breathing. But so that nothing would be lost entirely. The roads you came by were ours: we walked them to visit the lost.","When the Null began to follow our roads home, we drowned the archive and tore the index out of the Ledger, so the way could never be opened again. Three pages. I hid them, and then I forgot where. Will you find them?"],"waiting":"The Ledger lies open, and empty: {found} of {of} index pages found. They will be where the water could not reach.","ready":["The index. All three. Lay them in… there. Now the Ledger can be read again.","Read it with me. The last entries. I want to know who woke the roads."],"after":"You did not know. I can see that. But the roads are open because of that entry, and the Null walks them. Close what you can. Start with the Archivist. It was my friend, once.","cleared":"The water is stiller already. Past the archive the roads go on, into places even we never catalogued. Take care of the Ledger's last line. Write a better one."},"restored":{"title":"The Ledger Opens","pages":["The Ledger's pages turn by themselves: centuries of lost places in a hundred hands. A valley, a harbour, a hamlet with a bell. Then the entries stop, for a long, long time.","The last entry is new; the ink is barely dry. It names no place. It says: \"The road answers. I am going to see where the lost things go.\" The hand is yours. Ondine looks at you, and does not look away."]},"closing":{"title":"The Archive Sleeps","pages":["The tear folds shut, and the black water of the Drowned Archive lies still. On the Great Lectern the Ledger closes itself, gently, like a book someone means to come back to.","You know now whose hand woke the network. You do not yet know why, or what the Null wants with roads it never built. The answers are further out. So are the next rifts."]},"reward":{"xp":200,"items":[{"item":"rift-shard","count":3},{"item":"gem","count":1}]}}}
